# 🔒 PHI / security — NON-NEGOTIABLE (always on)

This app handles **Protected Health Information** (names, DOB, SSN, address,
contact info, Medicaid eligibility). Full rules + pre-flight checklist:
[`docs/ai/SECURITY-AND-PHI.md`](mdc:docs/ai/SECURITY-AND-PHI.md). **If a task would
relax any rule below, stop and flag it in your response — don't do it silently.**

1. **Never log PHI.** No names, DOB, SSN, address, phone, email, or raw answers in
   `logger.*`, `print`, errors, comments, or test fixtures. Log identifiers only
   (`session_id`, `field_key`, `event_type`, `source`, `confidence`).
2. **Never hardcode secrets.** Connection strings, API keys, JWT secrets,
   passwords live in `.env` only. Never commit `.env` / `.env.local`.
3. **EMR is read-only + parameterized.** Only `SELECT`, only `text()` with named
   bind params (see [`backend/app/emr/talbot_adapter.py`](mdc:backend/app/emr/talbot_adapter.py)).
   Never string-build SQL; never `INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/DDL`. Keep the
   `"IsDeleted" = false` soft-delete filter and graceful degradation.
4. **Mask at output.** Patient data leaving the backend uses the helpers in
   [`backend/app/core/security.py`](mdc:backend/app/core/security.py). Search returns
   `MaskedPatient`; full `EMRPatient` is **server-side only** — never serialize it
   to an HTTP response.
5. **Audit significant actions** via [`backend/app/core/audit.py`](mdc:backend/app/core/audit.py)
   with metadata passed through `sanitize_metadata`.
6. **Respect `sensitive: true`** fields in the form schema — never echo via TTS,
   never send their values to the LLM.
7. **Keep the disclaimer** on every page and PDF; keep the MOCK-mode banner.
8. **Don't loosen CORS or auth.** `ADMIN_PASSWORD` / `ADMIN_JWT_SECRET` defaults
   are insecure — require them via env, never hardcode a replacement.

Before finishing any change, run the pre-flight checklist in
[`docs/ai/SECURITY-AND-PHI.md`](mdc:docs/ai/SECURITY-AND-PHI.md#9-pre-flight-checklist-for-any-change).
